WEBVTT

00:04.810 --> 00:08.110
<i>With Iroha handling this, we can't fail.</i>

00:10.380 --> 00:13.620
<i>Go on, show them the very soul of acting!</i>

01:14.670 --> 01:20.350
<b>MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER HAS IT IN FOR ME!</b>

02:20.660 --> 02:25.620
<b>#11 "WE'RE PERFECT FOR TRAINING THE DRAMA CLUB"</b>

02:21.210 --> 02:25.270
<i>From that moment, our competition 
prep took off at lightning speed.</i>

02:25.890 --> 02:29.600
<i>First, I had Makigai Namako-sensei 
turn that ridiculous</i>

02:29.600 --> 02:32.040
<i>failed </i>Black Goat<i> script into a play.</i>

02:33.160 --> 02:36.590
<i>I knew I was asking a lot, 
so I was pretty nervous internally,</i>

02:36.590 --> 02:39.300
<i>but Makigai-sensei agreed immediately.</i>

02:39.300 --> 02:41.240
<i>It was finished in no time.</i>

02:40.550 --> 02:43.850
<b>05TH FLOOR ALLIANCE 
AKI: THANK YOU FOR THE REVISION. 
MAKIGAI NAMAKO: WAS THAT OKAY FOR YOU?</b>

02:42.280 --> 02:46.560
<i>Now, if we could just do something about 
that sparkly, saccharine fixation.</i>

02:43.850 --> 02:47.770
<b>AKI: YES, PERFECT! 
MAKIGAI NAMAKO: I'M IN THE SWING OF IT NOW, 
SO IF THAT'S GOOD ENOUGH, 
I'LL WRITE ALL YOU WANT!</b>

02:47.770 --> 02:49.560
<b>AKI: UH, GREAT. 
AKI: THANK YOU.</b>

02:49.560 --> 02:51.480
<i>For the stage backgrounds and lightning,</i>

02:51.480 --> 02:55.480
<i>Oz put together a backdrop creator 
program in the blink of an eye.</i>

02:56.110 --> 03:00.490
<i>It's rare for him to go all Ozuemon on me, 
but each time, I can't help but be impressed.</i>

03:00.980 --> 03:02.810
<i>For the sound effects and BGM,</i>

03:02.810 --> 03:07.490
<i>I had Otoi-san apply her skills 
to what the club already had.</i>

03:07.490 --> 03:09.500
<i>Those came out pretty great, too.</i>

03:11.060 --> 03:12.370
<i>The only hurdle left is...</i>

03:16.060 --> 03:18.010
What are you doing?!

03:18.010 --> 03:22.430
Oh! I'm sorry! I had something on my mind.

03:22.680 --> 03:25.520
Concentrate on the decorations!

03:26.580 --> 03:29.580
Is there something bothering you?

03:29.580 --> 03:30.390
What?

03:30.700 --> 03:33.530
If you don't mind talking to me, 
I am glad to listen.

03:33.530 --> 03:36.180
Sob, sob, sob...

03:38.280 --> 03:41.310
No! Why are you doing it that way?!

03:41.310 --> 03:43.020
Why?! Why, why, why?!

03:42.070 --> 03:44.530
<i>Imagine being able to get under </i>Iroha's<i> skin.</i>

03:44.530 --> 03:46.280
<i>Drama club, you're scary.</i>

03:46.280 --> 03:50.740
Midori-san, are you trying to play your part 
flawlessly from beginning to end?

03:50.740 --> 03:52.670
What? Isn't that what I'm supposed to do?

03:52.940 --> 03:56.060
No. You shouldn't try to get it
perfect from the get-go.

03:56.060 --> 04:00.260
Try to acclimate yourself 
to each line, one by one.

04:00.260 --> 04:01.790
Acclimate?

04:02.760 --> 04:06.440
You're trying so hard to recite 
your lines perfectly

04:06.440 --> 04:09.400
that you're stiffening up and 
making them sound unnatural.

04:10.830 --> 04:12.020
I get it!

04:12.560 --> 04:17.770
And Yamada-san, I think you can 
tone down the gesturing a bit.

04:12.560 --> 04:15.480
<i>Looks like Iroha's doing just fine.</i>

04:17.770 --> 04:18.740
Okay!

04:20.050 --> 04:21.830
Yamada-chan, are you okay?

04:23.000 --> 04:26.660
Oh, yeah. I'm just a little hungry.

04:26.920 --> 04:28.760
Should we take a short break?

04:28.760 --> 04:31.620
No! Let's run through that 
scene one more time!

04:31.940 --> 04:33.550
Right! Now...

04:35.120 --> 04:36.340
Stare...

04:37.490 --> 04:40.110
You've been peeking in on us almost every day.

04:40.110 --> 04:42.850
You don't have to wait for me, 
you know. You can go home.

04:42.850 --> 04:45.940
I haven't been waiting for you or anything.

04:46.780 --> 04:47.910
Here.

04:48.540 --> 04:51.670
For you. I made tuna sandwiches.

04:51.670 --> 04:53.970
O-Oh... Thanks.

04:53.970 --> 04:57.160
You always lose track of time when 
you get absorbed in something.

04:57.160 --> 04:59.820
Y-You need to take better care of yourself.

05:03.650 --> 05:07.340
Should you be doing stuff like this 
so openly when we're at school?

05:07.340 --> 05:09.370
People might get the wrong idea.

05:09.730 --> 05:13.520
We're not, you know, 
going out or anything.

05:13.520 --> 05:14.760
Are you stupid?

05:15.330 --> 05:18.750
We <i>are</i> going out. Here at school, at least.

05:20.020 --> 05:22.740
Also, what I said wasn't a joke.

05:23.810 --> 05:26.760
Like I told you...

05:27.890 --> 05:32.260
I <i>will</i> make you love me one day.

05:35.520 --> 05:40.310
So I'm going to be using <i>all</i> of 
my fake girlfriend privileges!

05:42.430 --> 05:44.740
Th-That's as far as I can go! Bye!

05:45.150 --> 05:46.360
Also, die!

05:46.970 --> 05:49.660
S-Sure. Be careful getting home.

05:50.830 --> 05:53.240
I'm looking forward to the play.

05:54.290 --> 05:55.800
O-Okay.

06:02.210 --> 06:05.170
Okay! You guys have gotten so much better!

06:05.690 --> 06:08.130
You thought so, too? We have, right?

06:08.130 --> 06:12.110
It's all thanks to you that 
we've been able to improve so much!

06:12.110 --> 06:14.200
Thank you, Instructor!

06:14.200 --> 06:16.180
We look forward to continuing tomorrow!

06:16.180 --> 06:19.480
Okay, everyone, great work today!

06:19.480 --> 06:21.720
We're in the final stretch 
before the competition!

06:21.720 --> 06:23.000
Let's knock 'em dead!

06:23.000 --> 06:24.900
Yeah!

06:48.260 --> 06:51.150
It's been another exhausting day, huh?

06:51.150 --> 06:54.930
Why are you flopping onto 
<i>my</i> bed like you own the place?

06:54.930 --> 07:01.060
Yours just feels more natural to me. It must 
be because I've been coming over every day.

07:01.060 --> 07:04.650
I feel like it's basically 
my own bed at this point!

07:08.210 --> 07:10.220
What's this now, Senpai?

07:10.220 --> 07:13.710
Are you curious about what's under my skirt?

07:13.710 --> 07:17.340
If you say, "I'm a perv who can't stop thinking 
about my friend's sister's underwear!"

07:17.340 --> 07:21.240
"Please allow me to see yours, Iroha-sama,"

07:21.240 --> 07:23.360
I might be willing to show you.

07:24.230 --> 07:27.600
Like hell, moron. I haven't the slightest 
interest in your underwear.

07:27.600 --> 07:31.300
Yeah, right! You <i>are</i> a guy, after all!

07:31.300 --> 07:32.590
You just can't help—

07:31.580 --> 07:32.590
Stop.

07:32.930 --> 07:37.780
Hey! No spraying me with deodorizer 
just because you're at a disadvantage!

07:37.780 --> 07:41.560
I can spray my own bed all I want.

07:39.310 --> 07:41.560
<b>WARNING: DO NOT SPRAY DIRECTLY AT OTHER PEOPLE.</b>

07:41.870 --> 07:44.940
If you don't like it, 
go back to your own place.

07:46.360 --> 07:48.570
Fine, fine. I get it.

07:50.110 --> 07:52.160
What? What are you plotting?

07:52.160 --> 07:54.240
Oh, what now?

07:54.240 --> 07:56.770
I do what you tell me to do, 
and you get suspicious.

07:56.770 --> 08:00.580
Are you just a little contrarian 
who really wants me to stay?

08:00.910 --> 08:05.500
Well, you seem tired, too, 
so I'll take off early this time.

08:07.710 --> 08:09.090
Did something happen?

08:10.510 --> 08:11.640
Huh?

08:11.640 --> 08:16.430
I mean, I just thought maybe something 
was bugging you about the drama club.

08:17.690 --> 08:20.350
Was it that obvious?

08:20.350 --> 08:24.250
When your teasing gets that weak? Yes.

08:24.250 --> 08:28.050
You're only half as obnoxious 
as usual right now.

08:28.050 --> 08:31.190
Oh, man! So <i>that's</i> what you based it on!

08:31.910 --> 08:37.030
How can you be so perceptive only 
at times like these? You're so unfair.

08:37.030 --> 08:38.960
Well? Let's hear it.

08:42.040 --> 08:45.670
I just felt a little envious of the drama club.

08:46.880 --> 08:51.920
They get to act on the stage, 
front and center, with their clubmates.

08:52.370 --> 08:55.740
I mean, I'm having fun doing the voices 
for <i>Black Goat</i>, of course.

08:55.740 --> 08:58.390
I've learned from it, and it's helped me grow.

08:58.780 --> 09:02.040
But I just can't help thinking about how,

09:02.040 --> 09:08.050
no matter how good I am, I'll always just be 
"Mysterious Voice Actor Brigade X."

09:08.050 --> 09:11.410
If I could say, "It's me! I'm doing this!"

09:11.410 --> 09:15.790
and speak proudly about 
what I do, it'd be so great.

09:15.790 --> 09:17.320
I can't help myself.

09:18.370 --> 09:20.240
Because then...

09:20.670 --> 09:24.750
I could really be a part 
of 05th Floor Alliance.

09:25.720 --> 09:28.250
<i>Yeah... She's right.</i>

09:28.670 --> 09:31.970
<i>It's obvious if I think about 
how she must feel.</i>

09:31.970 --> 09:34.510
<i>She doesn't have a place 
where she can show off her talent.</i>

09:35.400 --> 09:38.760
Then I'll put you out there 
in the open one day.

09:39.650 --> 09:44.840
We could even try some 2.5D media 
like what the drama club's doing.

09:44.840 --> 09:46.830
With you acting, of course.

09:46.830 --> 09:49.100
What? But that would...

09:49.100 --> 09:52.220
What do you think I made 
05th Floor Alliance for?

09:52.220 --> 09:57.860
It's a stage where you all can make the most 
of your talents without holding back.

09:57.860 --> 10:00.670
Now there'll be even more work 
I can give you in the future!

10:00.670 --> 10:02.500
This has been very productive!

10:02.500 --> 10:06.560
You're talking big, but just how 
much work are we talking here?

10:06.560 --> 10:10.210
Sorry to say it, but we run a real 
sweatshop in these parts.

10:10.210 --> 10:12.740
If it's what you want, I'll make it happen.

10:12.740 --> 10:15.210
So you'd better be ready!

10:20.780 --> 10:22.930
Roger that!

10:25.430 --> 10:27.980
All right, Iroha! 
The competition's not far off.

10:27.980 --> 10:30.650
We're at the critical point. 
No slacking off now!

10:30.650 --> 10:32.780
You got it, boss!

10:32.780 --> 10:36.820
You can expect great things from the 
legendary star instructor Iroha-san!

10:37.320 --> 10:39.780
This production is packed with my dreams!

10:39.780 --> 10:42.530
I'm gonna make it a success, no matter what!

10:43.210 --> 10:44.810
Yeah!

10:48.980 --> 10:50.520
<i>Who is it?</i>

10:52.290 --> 10:55.370
Reprint guaranteed! This is where "fun" lives!

10:55.370 --> 10:59.000
Whether it's comedy, drama, or tragedy, 
I'll bring out its glorious majesty, chirp!

10:59.000 --> 11:01.720
The idol editor of UZA Publishing...

11:03.570 --> 11:06.080
Kiraboshi Kanaria, age seventeen!

11:07.010 --> 11:10.110
Mashiro-chan! No violence, chirp!

11:10.600 --> 11:12.470
Shush!

11:14.340 --> 11:15.610
Oh, I get it!

11:16.000 --> 11:20.240
It's called "05th Floor Alliance" because 
you all live on the fifth floor, chirp!

11:20.240 --> 11:24.930
Remember that they have no idea 
that I'm Makigai Namako.

11:24.930 --> 11:26.570
Don't do anything careless.

11:26.570 --> 11:29.080
'Kay! I'll be a careful little birdie!

11:29.080 --> 11:31.040
<b>STAGE PLAY SCRIPT 
"CASTELLA IN THE CENTER, JAPANESE SWEETS 
IN THE RIGHT HAND, WESTERN SWEETS IN THE LEFT" 
BY MAKIGAI NAMAKO</b>

11:31.660 --> 11:35.660
Is this really a Makigai-sensei script, though?

11:35.660 --> 11:39.690
Yes. I think it came out pretty well. 
I'm kinda proud of it.

11:39.690 --> 11:43.040
Wait, what is this? 
You don't write like this! What happened?!

11:43.040 --> 11:45.010
I-Is there something odd about it?

11:45.010 --> 11:46.700
Anyone can tell it's chirping weird!

11:46.700 --> 11:52.330
This girly, lovey-dovey stuff is a 180-degree 
turn from the way you usually write, chirp!

11:52.330 --> 11:56.050
Your works are usually more... dark and creepy!

11:56.050 --> 11:59.190
They're like big, nasty bundles of resentment!

11:59.190 --> 12:00.970
You called them nasty.

12:00.970 --> 12:03.230
So how'd you end up writing <i>this</i>, chirp?!

12:03.230 --> 12:05.520
Darn it! And your deadline's so close!

12:05.520 --> 12:08.920
Just go back to being 
the old Makigai-sensei already!

12:10.120 --> 12:13.120
<b>MY FRIEND'S LITTLE SISTER HAS IT IN FOR ME!</b>

12:16.110 --> 12:18.630
<i>Tomorrow's the day of the competition,</i>

12:19.510 --> 12:22.550
<i>and today is our final rehearsal.</i>

12:26.620 --> 12:28.590
And that concludes our rehearsal.

12:28.590 --> 12:30.310
Thank you all!

12:35.470 --> 12:37.290
<i>It feels like it's been worth it.</i>

12:40.360 --> 12:41.740
<b>IROHA 
THAT MUST HAVE BEEN ROUGH, 
BUT YOUR INSTRUCTION CLEARLY PAID OFF 
IT'S LOOKING GOOD</b>

12:41.740 --> 12:44.990
<b>ISN'T IT? THIS IS WHAT 
YOUR IROHA-CHAN IS CAPABLE OF!</b>

12:44.990 --> 12:49.530
<b>FEEL FREE TO PRAISE ME FOREVER AND
 PAT MY HEAD LIKE I'M A DACHSHUND!</b>

12:49.530 --> 12:51.370
<b>DON'T GET AHEAD OF YOURSELF, IDIOT.</b>

12:53.940 --> 12:57.960
Yeah. They should fare pretty well 
in the competition now.

12:57.960 --> 13:00.920
Well, they're ready to be seen 
by an audience, at least.

13:01.510 --> 13:03.280
I knew you could do it, Ohboshi-kun.

13:03.280 --> 13:07.010
Only you could have brought that 
dysfunctional drama club this far.

13:07.010 --> 13:09.040
I didn't do anything.

13:09.040 --> 13:12.850
It was all down to the others' efforts 
plus the drama club's hard work.

13:13.340 --> 13:15.270
I need to thank you.

13:15.910 --> 13:17.690
No need for thanks.

13:18.020 --> 13:23.110
I just need <i>someone</i> to get 
her illustrations in by the deadline.

13:23.110 --> 13:25.840
O-Of course! That'd be great, wouldn't it?

13:25.840 --> 13:27.920
Also, we can't let our guard down yet.

13:27.920 --> 13:30.960
Whether they can win or not 
is a whole different story.

13:30.960 --> 13:35.080
So stay on top of those 
illustrations, would you?

13:35.080 --> 13:37.210
How did we go from thanks to threats?

13:37.210 --> 13:40.660
All I'm saying is that the gods 
are <i>always</i> watching.

13:40.660 --> 13:44.670
If you don't want to end up in trouble, be on 
your best behavior and meet your deadlines!

13:45.510 --> 13:49.180
I almost forgot! We're about to have 
a pep rally to psych us up for tomorrow!

13:49.620 --> 13:51.860
All of you should join in!

13:51.860 --> 13:54.430
I'm gonna head back and 
start getting things ready!

13:55.150 --> 13:56.260
<i>That bitch.</i>

13:56.260 --> 13:57.760
A pep rally, huh?

13:57.760 --> 14:01.330
We're not club members. 
Do you think it's okay for us to go?

14:01.330 --> 14:04.610
I guess so. It's a little late to 
distance ourselves like that now.

14:04.610 --> 14:06.330
Yeah? Maybe I'll go, then.

14:06.330 --> 14:08.840
Sure. I'll head there after I clean up.

14:08.840 --> 14:10.820
Go on back to the club room first.

14:10.820 --> 14:11.700
I could help.

14:12.000 --> 14:14.280
I've already made you do too much.

14:14.280 --> 14:16.590
At least let me handle the basic chores.

14:16.590 --> 14:18.830
Otherwise I'll have contributed nothing at all.

14:19.580 --> 14:23.210
You put this whole effort together. 
I'd say you've contributed plenty.

14:24.010 --> 14:26.990
Hey, by the way, how are 
things with Iroha lately?

14:26.990 --> 14:30.330
You had some trouble with her 
not too long ago. Did things work out?

14:30.330 --> 14:31.870
Yeah, thankfully.

14:31.870 --> 14:34.170
There's nothing really going on, though.

14:34.170 --> 14:37.480
We just went back to the status quo 
of her unlawfully entering my apartment.

14:37.480 --> 14:40.940
That makes me happy as a brother 
who wants his sister to be happy.

14:40.940 --> 14:44.320
I feel like Tsukinomori-san's been 
pretty aggressive lately, too.

14:44.320 --> 14:49.750
L-Like I told you before, it's just an act 
while she's my fake girlfriend.

14:49.750 --> 14:53.760
<i>I'm not in a place where I can sincerely 
face Mashiro's feelings right now.</i>

14:53.760 --> 14:56.790
<i>I'm not gonna put her feelings 
on blast just to joke around.</i>

14:56.790 --> 14:58.090
Huh...

14:58.090 --> 15:02.630
Well, okay. As your friend, I was kinda 
hoping for a love triangle, to be honest.

15:02.630 --> 15:05.960
Don't enjoy other people's struggles. 
That's messed up.

15:06.680 --> 15:09.060
I just think of it as a friend's privilege.

15:09.060 --> 15:10.430
Gimme a break.

15:14.680 --> 15:15.950
Ohboshi-kun...

15:17.320 --> 15:18.740
Do you have a moment?

15:19.770 --> 15:20.700
What's up?

15:20.700 --> 15:23.980
I just felt... like I should thank you.

15:24.360 --> 15:29.340
It's because of your help 
that we've improved so much.

15:29.340 --> 15:32.920
I'll admit, when you first showed up, 
I thought, "Who does he think he is?"

15:32.920 --> 15:35.330
But now, I'm glad you came along.

15:35.770 --> 15:36.350
So—

15:36.350 --> 15:37.300
Hold it.

15:37.910 --> 15:42.860
You and the drama club have improved 
 so much because of the work you all put in.

15:42.860 --> 15:44.710
I want to say that first and foremost.

15:45.130 --> 15:47.170
O-Okay...

15:47.900 --> 15:50.350
Also, I barely did anything.

15:50.350 --> 15:54.140
It was Instructor, Ozu, and Otoi-san 
who led you this far.

15:54.410 --> 15:57.560
And besides, you should save your thanks 
for after the competition.

15:59.920 --> 16:01.690
You're right. Okay.

16:02.430 --> 16:04.440
We'll give it our all tomorrow!

16:04.820 --> 16:07.020
Good. I'm rooting for you.

16:10.030 --> 16:15.570
Oh! But I'm still suspicious about you and 
Sumire-onee—I mean, Kageishi-sensei!

16:15.570 --> 16:18.030
I told you, it's all a misunderstanding.

16:18.030 --> 16:20.090
I won't believe you that easily!

16:20.090 --> 16:24.260
Sumire-oneechan is beautiful and badass! 
She must have tons of guys after her!

16:24.260 --> 16:26.580
I guess you could look at it that way.

16:26.580 --> 16:27.340
Besides...

16:27.340 --> 16:30.300
Earlier, you were just a little...

16:30.590 --> 16:31.660
A little what?

16:32.340 --> 16:33.380
N-Nothing!

16:33.780 --> 16:38.890
Anyway, don't you dare get up to anything 
s-s-sexy with Sumire-oneechan!

16:41.300 --> 16:45.260
Maybe she gets her weirdness 
from her big sister.

16:54.200 --> 16:55.130
What's going on?

16:56.680 --> 16:58.450
Yamada-chan passed out.

16:58.450 --> 16:59.390
What?!

16:59.800 --> 17:02.160
Now that I think about it, she...

17:07.480 --> 17:09.770
<i>She fought through it for that long?</i>

17:10.210 --> 17:14.240
I just took her to the nurse's office. 
She had a really high fever.

17:14.240 --> 17:18.510
They said someone from her family 
would take her to the hospital, but...

17:19.570 --> 17:23.350
I don't think she'll make it 
to the competition tomorrow.

17:24.650 --> 17:27.160
I should have tried harder to stop her.

17:27.160 --> 17:29.310
Damn it! I really blew it!

17:29.310 --> 17:34.190
No, it was my job to make sure 
all the members kept their health up.

17:34.190 --> 17:38.240
I knew she was the type to push 
herself too hard, and I...

17:40.700 --> 17:44.880
Enough. This isn't the time 
to be assigning blame.

17:44.880 --> 17:46.660
The competition is tomorrow.

17:46.990 --> 17:48.190
Right.

17:48.190 --> 17:51.590
Is there anyone who can stand in 
for Yamada-chan?

17:51.590 --> 17:54.770
I don't think I can. 
This is way too sudden.

17:54.770 --> 17:57.500
I couldn't memorize all her lines in one day.

17:57.500 --> 17:59.800
I could never take her place.

17:59.800 --> 18:02.790
I've only ever worked behind the scenes.

18:03.600 --> 18:08.140
Please! If we don't do something, 
we won't even be able to compete!

18:08.140 --> 18:11.190
And if we don't perform well, 
we'll be disbanded!

18:11.190 --> 18:15.020
No. We've worked so hard to make it this far.

18:15.020 --> 18:19.160
If we can't even compete, 
Yamada-chan will feel like it's her fault!

18:19.540 --> 18:21.400
I know, but...

18:21.400 --> 18:22.420
Still...

18:23.150 --> 18:27.660
We've worked so hard... all this time...

18:35.140 --> 18:36.920
<i>There is a solution.</i>

18:37.760 --> 18:39.280
<i>But it's something...</i>

18:40.080 --> 18:44.480
<i>I can't decide on my own.</i>

18:49.350 --> 18:51.650
Your acting ability is exceptional.

18:52.060 --> 18:54.080
And you can trust my judgment.

18:54.730 --> 18:57.990
Then I'll put you out there 
in the open one day.

18:57.990 --> 19:00.120
If it's what you want, I'll make it happen.

19:02.570 --> 19:03.860
I understand.

19:04.730 --> 19:05.790
Instructor?!

19:06.440 --> 19:07.390
<i>Iroha?</i>

19:12.720 --> 19:14.300
<i>Are you sure about this, Iroha?</i>

19:14.300 --> 19:17.460
<i>This means you're ready to put 
everything out there, right?</i>

19:17.460 --> 19:20.130
<i>This is what Senpai would do.</i>

19:20.130 --> 19:21.970
<i>Besides, I...</i>

19:22.370 --> 19:23.640
If you need a stand-in...

19:26.630 --> 19:28.180
I'll do it!

19:28.560 --> 19:30.630
What?! You're...

19:30.980 --> 19:32.220
Iroha...

19:33.370 --> 19:34.900
Kohinata-san?!

19:39.130 --> 19:41.780
<i>You</i> were our instructor, Kohinata-san?!

19:41.780 --> 19:45.410
I memorized all of the lines 
so I could help you guys out.

19:45.410 --> 19:47.740
I can pull off Yamada-san's part, no problem!

19:48.190 --> 19:52.140
But are you sure? 
This is the drama club's problem.

19:53.520 --> 19:55.950
Of course I'm sure!

19:55.950 --> 19:59.960
Hard work should only go 
unrewarded in shitty games!

20:00.430 --> 20:04.140
You're nothing like the rumors said you were.

20:04.140 --> 20:07.140
But it's just like how you were as Instructor...

20:07.140 --> 20:10.140
C'mon, don't sweat the little details!

20:10.140 --> 20:12.890
I don't want all of your hard work 
to go to waste!

20:13.320 --> 20:16.690
Besides, my dream is riding on this play, too.

20:17.320 --> 20:18.180
Your dream?

20:18.180 --> 20:19.860
But enough talk!

20:19.860 --> 20:22.610
Will you let me help you or not?

20:22.610 --> 20:25.240
Let's hear your decision, Midori-san!

20:29.950 --> 20:30.870
Kohinata-san...

20:31.730 --> 20:34.250
No... Instructor!

20:35.330 --> 20:36.210
Yes!

20:37.270 --> 20:39.000
Please help us!

20:40.210 --> 20:41.220
Sure!

20:41.220 --> 20:45.130
Let's take Yamada-chan's spirit 
with us to victory!

20:45.130 --> 20:48.720
I'll show you some Hollywood-worthy acting,

20:48.720 --> 20:50.740
drama club peeps!

20:52.110 --> 20:55.460
<i>That's the way, Iroha. If that's what 
you've made up your mind to do,</i>

20:54.230 --> 20:58.110
<b>AIM TO WIN REGIONALS!</b>

20:55.460 --> 20:57.180
<i>I'll be right there with you!</i>

20:58.650 --> 21:02.530
<b>Translation: Becky Cottrill</b>

21:02.900 --> 21:05.990
<b>Subtitle Editing: Geoff Mazzolini
Subtitle Timing: Krzysztof Kunc</b>

21:06.530 --> 21:09.870
<b>Quality Control: Gabriella Ramirez
Translation Check: David Saylor</b>

22:31.410 --> 22:33.530
Iroha acts, huh?

22:33.530 --> 22:36.560
I had no idea she was 
hiding things from me, too.

22:36.560 --> 22:39.150
Sorry I didn't tell you sooner.

22:39.150 --> 22:41.040
Nah, you couldn't help it.

22:41.040 --> 22:43.340
She'd be in trouble if Mom found out.

22:43.700 --> 22:47.620
And I know the drama club isn't 
the only thing she's had a hand in.

22:48.260 --> 22:50.910
She's done work for 
05th Floor Alliance, too, hasn't she?

22:52.610 --> 22:55.680
Yeah. I'm not going to hide it any longer.

22:55.680 --> 22:56.500
I see.

22:56.500 --> 23:01.660
I guess you were even more important 
to Iroha than I realized, huh?

23:01.660 --> 23:03.190
That's a stretch.

23:03.490 --> 23:05.190
I don't think so.

23:05.550 --> 23:08.190
You're the only one for her.

23:08.460 --> 23:11.240
I'm fully convinced of that now.

23:21.250 --> 23:26.250
<b>WATCH AGAIN NEXT TIME <3</b>
